# G128 — Screen Saver

*v2. See `screen-saver.md` for prose: six-state idle FSM with mixed triggers,
integer-scaled 2D physics with elastic reflection, dim opacity derived not
stored, activity resets but doesn't unlock Locked.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Idle Guardian

[idle-guardian @config
    IN ORDER TO
        dim the display after @config:idle-ms of inactivity
        run an animated screen saver after the dim completes
        auto-lock the session after @config:auto-lock-ms of saver time
        wake on activity from Dimming or Saver but require unlock from Locked

    @saver <- [ss[new-saver {config: @config}]]

    for @i in 0..5
        [ss[add-line {saver: @saver,
                       line: {p1: {x: [rand 0 192000], y: [rand 0 108000],
                                    vx: [rand -10000 10000], vy: [rand -10000 10000]}
                               p2: {x: [rand 0 192000], y: [rand 0 108000],
                                    vx: [rand -10000 10000], vy: [rand -10000 10000]}
                               color: {r: 0, g: 255, b: 255}}}]]

    until @shutdown [
        at @every 16 ms
            [ss[tick {saver: @saver, ms: 16}]]
            where @saver:state is "saver"
                #canvas @saver
            where @saver:state is "dimming"
                #fade-to-black opacity: @saver:dim-opacity

        sync @input
            -> [ss[record-activity {saver: @saver}]]

        sync @auth-approved
            -> [ss[unlock {saver: @saver}]]
    ]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[ss
    new-saver        {config}
    add-line         {saver, line}
    tick             {saver, ms}
    record-activity  {saver}
    unlock           {saver}
    dim-opacity      {saver}                ;; 0..255 (derived from state-time)
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: activity has contextual effect

The v1 spec surfaced "activity has three contextual effects" as a
design finding. In Innate, that's the natural shape of resolver
dispatch:

[ss[record-activity {saver: @saver}
    where
        in "active" state this resets the idle timer
        and in "dimming" or "saver" states this transitions to "waking"
        and in "locked" state this has no effect
            because security boundaries must not be bypassed by keypresses
        and in "waking" state this keeps the wake progressing
]

Same event, different resolver behavior per state. The constraint
documents the security contract explicitly.

---

## Physics integration gated to saver state

[ss[tick {saver: @saver, ms: @ms}
    where physics integration runs only when state is "saver"
        because animating during "dimming" wastes CPU on a fading screen
        and animating during "active" wastes CPU on a visible desktop
        and animating during "locked" / "waking" is irrelevant to the user
]

---

## Reflection as energy-preserving constraint

[line-endpoint @ep @canvas-width @canvas-height
    where
        the endpoint's new position is old-position + velocity × ms
        and if the new x < 0, reflect: new-x = -new-x, vx = -vx
        and if the new x > canvas-width × 100, reflect similarly
        and the same for y against canvas-height × 100
        and speed is preserved (only direction flips)
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @cfg <- {idle-ms: 1000, dim-ms: 200, auto-lock-ms: 500, wake-ms: 100,
              canvas-width: 100, canvas-height: 100}
    @s <- [ss[new-saver {config: @cfg}]]

    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "active"
    [ss[tick {saver: @s, ms: 1100}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "dimming"
    -> @s:dim-opacity              ;; -> 0 (just entered)

    [ss[tick {saver: @s, ms: 100}]]
    -> @s:dim-opacity              ;; -> 127 (half of dim-ms)

    [ss[tick {saver: @s, ms: 100}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "saver"

    [ss[tick {saver: @s, ms: 600}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "locked"

    [ss[record-activity {saver: @s}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "locked" (unchanged; activity can't unlock)

    [ss[unlock {saver: @s}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "waking"

    [ss[tick {saver: @s, ms: 150}]]
    -> @s:state                    ;; -> "active"
]
